    "evidence_text": "Fort Berens\n\nAnjanvel\n\nFort Kongenstein\n\nFort Kongenstein (Danish: \"Fort Kongensten\" ) was a Danish trading fort located in Ada Foah, Ghana built in 1783.\n\nAda Foah\n\nFort Dansborg\n\n The fort is the second largest Danish fort after Kronborg.\n\n The fort is now used as a museum where the major artifacts of the fort and the Danish empire are displayed.\n\nFort Koshkonong\n\n General Henry Atkinson was the commander of the fort during the war.\n\n The original fort was abandoned by the Army following the conflict.\n\n Local settlers dismantled it for the wood as the town developed.\n\nFort Anderson (North Carolina)\n\n It was used as a Confederate Fort during the American Civil War.\n\n The fort was pivotal in protecting the Cape Fear River inlets and Wilmington upstream.\n\nFort Saint-Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric\n\nPrinces Town, Ghana\n\n Because the Fort Gro\u00df Friedrichsburg was named after a Prince, it has been referred to as: Ft. Friedrichsburg/Princes Town.\n\n The fort was to be the headquarters of the Brandenburgers in Africa.\n\nMuskwa River\n\n The river rises at Fern Lake in the Bedaux Pass in the Northern Rocky Mountains.\n\n The region is a popular wilderness recreation destination.",
